1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,591
Calculator apps make you fight the keys.

2
00:00:03,711 --> 00:00:07,660
Units need another app, and graphs yet another.

3
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:11,730
QCalc puts it all in one scientific calculator.

4
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:16,962
Type math the way you write it on paper.

5
00:00:17,082 --> 00:00:21,894
Keep the units, as in 60 mph to km/h,

6
00:00:22,014 --> 00:00:25,730
or solve an equation, or an integral.

7
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:31,880
Answers can stay exact, with fractions, roots and π.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,730
With more precision, you get up to 200,000 digits.

9
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:41,280
Everyday calculations are in Tools.

10
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:49,730
The price tool works out a discount and tax: just tap an example.

11
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:56,134
The loan tool gives the monthly payment, the interest and the table.

12
00:00:56,254 --> 00:01:01,730
There are tools for splitting a bill, dates and hours too.

13
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:10,683
On the conversion screen, type a number and it converts at once:

14
00:01:10,803 --> 00:01:15,730
length, weight, temperature, fuel economy and currencies.

15
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:21,601
Draw two functions in the 2D graph and tap ⟳ 3D:

16
00:01:21,721 --> 00:01:27,172
the region turns into a solid of revolution, with its volume.

17
00:01:27,292 --> 00:01:31,730
Viewing it in 3D is a QCalc Pro feature.

18
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:37,901
Tap an axis to turn the region around it,

19
00:01:38,021 --> 00:01:45,730
and show the disks or shells that add up to the volume.

20
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:51,295
QCalc Pro takes the positions and diameters you measured,

21
00:01:51,415 --> 00:01:57,730
gives the volume, capacity and weight, and saves an STL file.

22
00:01:58,150 --> 00:02:05,730
It also finds the liquid in a tank from its level.

23
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:11,985
Calculation notes work a line at a time, with a total.

24
00:02:12,105 --> 00:02:16,858
You can name values, like rent = 1450 USD.

25
00:02:16,978 --> 00:02:21,730
The history can be searched, pinned and added up.

26
00:02:22,150 --> 00:02:30,977
Tap ? on a screen to open its page of the user manual.

27
00:02:31,097 --> 00:02:33,730
The manual works offline.

28
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:38,686
Everything is calculated on your phone, and no personal data is collected.

29
00:02:38,806 --> 00:02:43,730
Math as you write it, from graphs to 3D solids. This is QCalc.

